Never trust a slaver, because you never know when they might "get a bunch of guys" to "wait around back" and sell you to the highest price.

Never trust a death cultist, because you never know when they might feed you to their awakening god. But, if you're worried about what awaits you, they just might know how to abate [your demise, but pronounced you]

Never trust a kinslayer, because you never know when "kin" and mercy fail to coincide. We are all family here. Everyone has the same ancestors. We all eat the same bread.

You can trust gamblers. They're always there when you need them, and unfortunately, never there when you need them, but they won't betray you, because they want all the odds on their side.

You can trust martyrs, they will always take on new burdens and push forward, no matter the cost. But don't let them make all the decisions, because you never know when they might sacrifice you as the next certain cost.

Never trust a sith, because you never know when your pain is their seductive delight. Their entire path to power is oriented around "giving in to temptation", and they are known for their cruelty. Do the math.

You can trust a wizard, they are always waiting on something or someone else. But, they know just what to say to get you up and out of the house, so c'mon let's get going, daylight's burning and midnight's turning.

Trust those who lead by example to either continue as such, or falter, but do not expect more from them. Trust those who are inventive in design to always approach from another angle, but don't let them lead the central push.

Trust those with experience to try more of the same, and trust the youth to always get up and try a-gain.

Never trust someone who says never a lot. Only those with no hope would relinquish the possibility of alternatives. There is always another way. Hope is always in play.